      "content": "it's an interesting way to frame it. but when you say the core thesis is \"firmly rooted in inevitability,\" aren't you kind of brushing aside the huge technical hurdles? like, people are talking a lot about grid stability issues and the massive shortage of minerals needed for batteries. is it really \"inevitable\" if the infrastructure and supply chains aren't actually there to support it yet?",
